 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The session cookie holds the member and the session's expiry, signed with the key in `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`
+([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)). Every web server holds the same
+key, so any of them accepts the cookie and a deploy logs no one out. A cookie whose signature does not match, or whose
+expiry has passed, logs no one in. Nothing about a session is stored on the server.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A member cannot be logged out from the server before their session expires. Workaround: wait out the 30 minutes.
+- Rotating `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` logs out every member. Workaround: rotate it only between pickups.
+- A server started without `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` falls back to the key `dev-only`, which is in the repository: anyone
+  can then sign a cookie for any member, and its cookies fail on servers holding the real key. Workaround: check the
+  variable is in the deploy secrets before a server starts.
 
